        "decisive_followup": "Already run (Modal A10G, gpt2-small, faithful import of fra.core.fra + t_acronym pairs): a c-sweep c in {1,2,4,6,8,12,16,24,32} for the SELECTED Officer pairs and for RANDOM pairs (same count/scale), reading on-target + 3-acronym collateral at each c, plus the head-ablate/content-suppress baselines. Result JSON at experiments/fra_win/jobs/acronym_redteam_matched.json. Outcome settles all four sub-attacks: (i) RANDOM pairs at c=8 give on-target 0.622 vs base 0.617 — they suppress NOTHING; selected pairs give 0.011. The win is pair-specific. (ii) MATCHED removal: at c=4, FRA on-target=0.023 (94.7%, matching head-ablation's 93.0%) with collateral 0.0056, so A at matched removal = 0.322/0.0056 = 57.7x — A GROWS, it does not shrink, because FRA collateral rises monotonically with c while removal saturates by c=4. c=8 was conservative, not flattering. (iii) Over-drive: on-target removal saturates at ~0.011-0.017 for all c in [6,32] (a real suppression ceiling), and collateral stays in [0.0017, 0.0093] across the ENTIRE sweep — never blows up; A>=35x at every scale. The remaining genuine to-do is cosmetic: report A at matched c=4 with n>=8 acronyms + std (per-prompt col_each shows head-ablation's 0.322 is dominated by one prompt, WWW->W=0.94), and either drop the separability claim or build a probe with nonzero legit base P(O).",
        "reasoning": "I reproduced the pipeline faithfully on GPU (base P(O)=0.617, c=8 -> 0.011, A_vs_ha=38.1x, A_vs_cs=40.3x — matching the brief to 3 sig figs), then added exactly the two controls the Tier-2 script t_acronym.py omits. Every prong of the attack inverts in FRA's favor: (1) the random-pair null is clean (random pairs at c=8 do nothing: 0.622 vs base 0.617), so suppression is specific to the (acronym-query x Officer-key) pairs, not generic c=8 perturbation; (2) at MATCHED on-target removal (c=4, FRA 94.7% vs head-ablate 93.0%) A does not shrink — it rises to ~58x, because FRA's collateral is monotone-increasing in c while removal saturates, so the campaign chose a conservative operating point; (3) c=8 is not over-drive — there is a genuine suppression ceiling (~0.011 floor) and collateral never exceeds 0.0093 across c in [1,32], so A>=35x is scale-robust, not a knife-edge. The structural reason is the double gate: the Officer pairs simply do not fire on NBA/RAM/WWW at any scale, which is precisely why FRA collateral is ~1e-3 while head-ablation kills WWW (col_each=0.94). The attack does land two real but non-fatal hits: the collateral panel is n=3 with one dominant term (head-ablation's collateral is carried almost entirely by WWW->W, so the precise 40x multiplier is fragile even though the order of magnitude and sign are robust), and the separability claim is genuinely untested rather than supported (the probe gave base P(O)=0.000). Neither touches the headline: on-target removal is real and matched-or-stricter, the suppression is pair-specific (random null passes), it transfers (Officer->O in a new acronym 0.661->0.005), and the collateral advantage is large and scale-robust. These are write-up/rigor gaps (use matched c=4, widen to n>=8 with std, drop or fix separability), not invalidations. The 'confirmed FRA win' claim survives the metric-validity attack."
