        "reasoning": "I reproduced the result from scratch on gpt2-small (after fixing a BOS-prepend tokenization landmine that silently broke the probe): base P(O)=0.617 and LBNR R=0.955 match the campaign exactly, so the behavior and screen are real. Attack A: independent causal edge-cut confirms 3/4 paper heads (10.10 dP=0.403, 8.11 0.334, 9.9 0.132) ARE the true load-bearers — they were validated, not assumed; honest blemishes are that 11.4 is causally dead (dP=0.003, harmlessly carried) and 10.6 (dP=0.111) is a real extra head outside the named set, neither of which undermines the win. Attack B: I confirmed on-target is non-discriminating (FRA ties the position-patch), so the win cannot rest there. Attack C (the core confound): I ran the discriminating tests live and they REFUTE the position-cut hypothesis in two independent ways — (i) transfer with Officer moved to a new position: FRA suppresses (0.646->0.055) while a position-patch at the old slot fails (0.640); (ii) my own swap-content-same-slot control gives a textbook double dissociation in the opposite direction from my attack. The edit is genuinely content-addressed. Hardening: faithful scale c~2 already yields 86% removal (not a c=8 over-drive artifact), and the effect is distributed across 3 heads/layers, so it does not hinge on a single SAE/layer choice. Novelty: mechanistically distinct from induction — induction routes by a positional prev-token-match key, whereas acronym letter-movers route by a content conjunction (acronym-query x specific-capitalized-word key) and copy via OV; the swap-control dissociation is precisely the signature that would NOT appear for a positional induction key. The only genuine deficiency is process hygiene, not substance: the transfer-FRA number was hardcoded and no JSON was saved, but I recomputed it and the conclusion stands. Verdict: survives; not fatal; the swap-content control is the one experiment to bank it."
